n- **histograma del WER por audio** y los **10 peores casos** (referencia y transcripción), solo sobre el split de desarrollo.\n\n**Cómo leerlo:** un WER bajo no garantiza que se conserve la intención: lo que importa para el TP es si los errores caen sobre palabras de las que depende la intención o las entidades. Esa relación se analiza en las secciones 10 a 12. El audio es habla leída y limpia, por lo que este WER es optimista frente a habla espontánea.\n\n**Salida esperada:** tabla de WER global por split, tabla por escenario, histograma y tabla de peores casos.","metadata":{}},{"cell_type":"code","source":"for sp in SPLITS_AUDIO:\n    d = MATCHED[sp]\n    w = wer_per_audio(d[\"norm_ref\"], d[\"whisper_norm\"])\n    for c in [\"S\", \"D\", \"I\", \"N\", \"wer\"]:\n        d[c] = w[c].values\n\nrows = []\nfor sp in SPLITS_AUDIO:\n    d = MATCHED[sp]\n    rows.append({\"split\": sp, \"audios\": len(d), \"palabras ref (N)\": int(d[\"N\"].sum()), \"S\": int(d[\"S\"].sum()), \"D\": int(d[\"D\"].sum()), \"I\": int(d[\"I\"].sum()),\n                 \"WER global\": corpus_wer(d), \"WER medio por audio\": d[\"wer\"].mean(),\n                 \"% audios con WER=0\": 100 * (d[\"wer\"] == 0).mean(),\n                 \"WER jiwer (control)\": jiwer_check(list(d[\"norm_ref\"]), list(d[\"whisper_norm\"]))})\ndisplay(pd.DataFrame(rows).set_index(\"split\").round(4))\n\nd = MATCHED[DEV_SPLIT]\nby_sc = pd.DataFrame({sc: {\"audios\": len(g), \"WER global\": corpus_wer(g), \"WER medio por audio\": g[\"wer\"].mean()} for sc, g in d.groupby(\"scenario_name_ref\")}).T\ndisplay(by_sc.sort_values(\"WER global\", ascending=False).round(4))\n\nfig, ax = plt.subplots(figsize=(8, 3.5))\nax.hist(d[\"wer\"].dropna().clip(upper=1.5), bins=HIST_BINS)\nax.set_title(f\"WER por audio ({DEV_SPLIT}); valores > 1.5 se agrupan en 1.5\"); ax.set_xlabel(\"WER\"); ax.set_ylabel(\"audios\")\nplt.tight_layout(); plt.show()\n\nprint(f\"Los {N_WORST} peores casos ({DEV_SPLIT}):\")\ndisplay(d.sort_values(\"wer\", ascending=False).head(N_WORST)[[\"id\", \"utt_ref\", \"whisper_raw\", \"wer\"]].round(3).reset_index(drop=True))","metadata":{"trusted":true,"execution":{"iopub.status.busy":"2026-11-23T21:39:41.736064Z","iopub.execute_input":"2026-11-23T21:39:41.7365Z","iopub.status.idle":"2026-11-23T21:39:42.038256Z","shell.execute_reply.started":"2026-11-23T21:39:41.736476Z","shell.execute_reply":"2026-11-23T21:39:42.037704Z"}},"outputs":[{"output_type":"display_data","data":{"text/plain":"            audios  palabras ref (N)    S    D    I  WER global  WER medio por audio  % audios con WER=0  WER jiwer (control)\nsplit                                                                                                                        \nvalidation    2033             14503  792  160  119      0.0738               0.0902             70.0935               0.0738","text/html":"<div>\n<style scoped>\n    .dataframe tbody tr th:only-of-type {\n        vertical-align: middle;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe tbody tr th {\n        vertical-align: top;\n    }\n\n    .dataframe thead th {\n        text-align: right;\n    }\n</style>\n<table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\">\n  <thead>\n    <tr style=\"text-align: right;\">\n      <th></th>\n      <th>audios</th>\n      <th>palabras ref (N)</th>\n      <th>S</th>\n      <th>D</th>\n      <th>I</th>\n      <th>WER global</th>\n      <th>WER medio por audio</th>\n      <th>% audios con WER=0</th>\n      <th>WER jiwer (control)</th>\n    </tr>\n    <tr>\n      <th>split</th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n      <th></th>\n    </tr>\n  </thead>\n  <tbody>\n    <tr>\n      <th>validation</th>\n      <td>2033</td>\n      <td>14503</td>\n      <td>792</td>\n      <td>160</td>\n      <td>119</td>\n      <td>0.0738</td>\n      <td>0.0902</td>\n      <td>70.0935</td>\n      <td>0.0738</td>\n    </tr>\n  </tbody>\n</table>\n</div>"},"metadata":{}}